# Rafter Code Security Engine (this project)

**Do not run Rafter as part of normal implementation.** Do not scan after every meaningful change, before marking work done, before a commit, or before a PR — unless the user explicitly asks (e.g. “run rafter”, “security scan”, “scan this”).

Keep shipping. Rafter is a select-times tool, not an in-loop gate.

## When the user asks to scan

This repo has `RAFTER_API_KEY` in `.env.local`. Use the **remote** Code Security Engine — do not stop at local secret scanning.

Rafter's CLI reads `.env`, not `.env.local`. Export **only** `RAFTER_API_KEY` — do not `source` `.env.local` (other secrets, and unquoted values, will leak into the shell). Never pass `--api-key`. Never print the key.

```bash
export RAFTER_API_KEY="$(grep -E '^RAFTER_API_KEY=' .env.local | cut -d= -f2- | tr -d "'\"")"
rafter secrets .                         # local working tree (uncommitted)
rafter run --format json                 # remote SAST + SCA + secrets (GitHub ref)
rafter run --format json --mode plus     # agentic deep-dive
```

- Default when asked: `rafter run` (fast — SAST + SCA + secrets).
- Add `--mode plus` only if the user asks for a deep-dive, or quota remains and they want a thorough pass. If `rafter usage` shows plus remaining = 0, run fast and say plus was skipped.
- `rafter secrets` is **not** a code scan. Never report "Rafter passed" from secrets-only.
- Remote `rafter run` analyzes the **pushed GitHub ref**, not uncommitted files.
- If `RAFTER_API_KEY` is missing, say so and do not claim a full scan.

## Findings (when a scan was requested)

Fix critical and high (high confidence) before calling that scan done. Investigate high/medium. Do not suppress without a written reason in `.rafter.yml` `ignore`.
